      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"Reset: the anti-brick core's boot ROM starts here. Turns interrupts off, selects interrupt\nmode 1 and goes to the start-up code; interrupts stay off from then on"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "11": {"synopsis":"The compiler's name, in ASCII: \"Z88DK\""},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "19": {"synopsis":"The compiler's version, in ASCII and ended by a zero byte: \"2.20\""},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "27": {"synopsis":"Takes 3 from DE. Not called in this ROM\nEntry: DE = the value.\nExit: DE = the value - 3.\nChanges: DE."},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "35": {"synopsis":"Takes 3 from BC. Not called in this ROM\nEntry: BC = the value.\nExit: BC = the value - 3.\nChanges: BC."},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "43": {"synopsis":"Drops three words from the stack and returns. Not reached in this ROM"},
        "46": {"synopsis":"A lone RET: the unused restarts jump here to return to their caller"},
        "48": {"synopsis":"RST $30: not used; returns at once\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "51": {"synopsis":"$FD: the first byte of a JP (IY) that is never run; CALL $0034 runs the JP (HL) it hides"},
        "52": {"synopsis":"CALL $0034 calls the routine whose address is in HL\nEntry: HL = the routine's address.\nChanges: whatever the routine changes."},
        "53": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the address in IX. Not reached in this ROM"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"RST $38 and the mode 1 interrupt: re-enables interrupts and returns. Interrupts are never\nenabled in this ROM, but the $FF bytes after the code would each run RST $38\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "59": {"synopsis":"Stores A in the 16 bytes from HL. Not called in this ROM\nEntry: A = the value; HL = the first byte.\nExit: HL = the byte after the last one.\nChanges: HL."},
        "92": {"synopsis":"Adds 8 to HL. Not called in this ROM\nEntry: HL = the value.\nExit: HL = the value + 8.\nChanges: HL."},
        "102": {"synopsis":"NMI: returns at once (RETN)"},
        "105": {"synopsis":"The start-up code: sets the stack to the top of memory, copies the six start values to\n$5B00-$5B05, clears the 1134 bytes of variables at $5B06-$5F73, runs MAIN, and stops when it\nreturns","comment":"SP = $0000: the first push goes to $FFFF"},
        "108": {"comment":"From the start values after the texts"},
        "120": {"comment":"The variables to clear"},
        "126": {"comment":"With 0"},
        "134": {"synopsis":"Stops the processor for good: interrupts are off, so the HALT is never left. EXIT and the\nend of START come here","comment":"Keeps HL as it is"},
        "137": {"synopsis":"Halts again should the processor ever leave the HALT"},
        "139": {"synopsis":"Gives the screen address of a character cell's top pixel row, the cell given on the stack.\nThe caller pushes the cell and calls; the routine takes the cell off the stack\nEntry: on the stack, the cell: low byte = the column (0-31), high byte = the row (0-23).\nExit: HL = the screen address.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "140": {"comment":"HL = the cell; the return address goes in its place"},
        "144": {"synopsis":"Gives the screen address of a character cell's top pixel row\nEntry: L = the column (0-31); H = the row (0-23).\nExit: HL = the screen address.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "148": {"comment":"The row's low 3 bits, as bits 7-5"},
        "153": {"comment":"The row's third of the screen, as bits 4-3 of the high byte"},
        "159": {"synopsis":"Sets the border colour: keeps it in the copy of port $FE at $5B00 and sends the copy out\nEntry: L = the colour (bits 2-0 are used).\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, L."},
        "187": {"synopsis":"Marks a failure: stores 255 in the error number at $5B06 and returns -1 with carry set.\nDivision by zero comes here\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = $FFFF; carry set.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "200": {"synopsis":"Returns -1 with carry set\nExit: HL = $FFFF; carry set.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "205": {"synopsis":"The mode 1 interrupt's handler: enables interrupts and returns"},
        "208": {"synopsis":"The NMI's handler: returns from the NMI"},
        "210": {"synopsis":"Negates DE\nEntry: DE = the value.\nExit: DE = -value.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "218": {"synopsis":"Negates HL\nEntry: HL = the value.\nExit: HL = -value.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "226": {"synopsis":"Signed 16-bit division of two words on the stack, which the routine takes off: the caller\npushes the divisor, then the dividend, and calls\nEntry: on the stack, the dividend on top, the divisor under it.\nExit: HL = the quotient; DE = the remainder.\nError: division by zero gives 32767 or -32768 (the dividend's sign) and stores 255 at $5B06.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "233": {"synopsis":"Signed 16-bit remainder of two words on the stack, which the routine takes off: the caller\npushes the divisor, then the dividend, and calls\nEntry: on the stack, the dividend on top, the divisor under it.\nExit: HL = the remainder (the dividend's sign); DE = the quotient.\nError: division by zero, as DIV_ARGS.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "242": {"synopsis":"32-bit multiplication of two long words on the stack, which the routine takes off: the\ncaller pushes each one high word first, and calls\nEntry: on the stack, one long word on top, the other under it.\nExit: DEHL = the product's low 32 bits.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "243": {"comment":"DEHL' = the long word on top"},
        "254": {"synopsis":"Signed 16-bit division: divides the magnitudes, then gives the quotient the sign of the\ntwo operands' signs combined and the remainder the dividend's sign\nEntry: HL = the dividend; DE = the divisor.\nExit: HL = the quotient; DE = the remainder.\nError: division by zero, as DIV_ARGS.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "256": {"comment":"Dividing by 0?"},
        "258": {"comment":"B = the dividend's sign; C = the divisor's"},
        "275": {"comment":"Signs differ?"},
        "280": {"comment":"Dividend positive?"},
        "286": {"synopsis":"SDIV16 by zero: marks the failure and gives 32767, or -32768 for a negative dividend"},
        "292": {"comment":"Dividend positive?"},
        "302": {"synopsis":"Unsigned 16-bit division\nEntry: HL = the dividend; DE = the divisor, not 0.\nExit: HL = the quotient; DE = the remainder; carry clear.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL."},
        "304": {"comment":"Divisor below 256?"},
        "306": {"comment":"A = the dividend's low byte; HL = its high byte"},
        "310": {"comment":"The quotient has at most 8 bits"},
        "312": {"synopsis":"UDIV16 with a divisor of 256 or more: one quotient bit per pass, 8 passes"},
        "315": {"comment":"Divisor fits?"},
        "320": {"synopsis":"The next pass; A gathers the quotient's bits inverted","comment":"Carry = the quotient bit"},
        "334": {"synopsis":"UDIV16 with a divisor below 256: 16 passes, the remainder in A","comment":"A = the remainder so far"},
        "338": {"synopsis":"One quotient bit: shifts the next dividend bit into A"},
        "340": {"comment":"A went past 8 bits?"},
        "342": {"comment":"Below the divisor?"},
        "345": {"synopsis":"Takes the divisor from A and sets the quotient bit"},
        "347": {"synopsis":"The next pass; then DE = the remainder"},
        "352": {"synopsis":"Division by zero: marks the failure and returns -1"},
        "356": {"synopsis":"MUL32 when both high words are 0: a 16 by 16 bit multiplication"},
        "362": {"synopsis":"32-bit multiplication with the Z80N's MUL, keeping the product's low 32 bits\n1. Both high words 0: MUL16X16 does it.\n2. Otherwise the 8 by 8 bit products that reach the low 32 bits are added up.\nEntry: DEHL = one factor; DEHL' = the other.\nExit: DEHL = the product's low 32 bits; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "368": {"comment":"Both high words 0?"},
        "472": {"synopsis":"16 by 16 bit multiplication with the Z80N's MUL: four 8 by 8 bit products\nEntry: HL and DE = the factors.\nExit: DEHL = the 32-bit product.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "505": {"synopsis":"Unsigned division of a 32-bit dividend by a 16-bit divisor, which must not be 0: 32 passes\nof shift and subtract over both register sets. Called with carry clear\nEntry: DEHL = the dividend; BC = the divisor; carry clear.\nExit: DEHL = the quotient; DEHL' = the remainder.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "507": {"comment":"DEHL' = the divisor"},
        "511": {"comment":"Carry set: check for 0 first"},
        "518": {"synopsis":"Dividing by 0?"},
        "524": {"synopsis":"Sets up the passes: the dividend's low word in BC and its high word in BC' and A, the\nremainder (0) in HL and HL'"},
        "541": {"synopsis":"One pass: shifts the next dividend bit into the remainder and tries to take the divisor off"},
        "562": {"comment":"Divisor fitted?"},
        "569": {"synopsis":"Carry = the quotient bit, shifted in at the next pass"},
        "590": {"synopsis":"Division by zero: marks the failure and returns -1"},
        "594": {"synopsis":"Beeps, the pitch and length given on the stack, which the routine takes off: the caller\npushes the frequency, then the length, and calls\nEntry: on the stack, the length in ms on top, the frequency in Hz under it.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "600": {"synopsis":"Beeps through the speaker bit of port $FE\n1. The number of cycles is frequency * length / 1000.\n2. The delay for half a cycle is 437500 / frequency - 30, in the loop's units.\nEntry: HL = the frequency in Hz; DE = the length in ms.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "604": {"comment":"Frequency * length / 1000: the cycles"},
        "615": {"comment":"437500: the loop's units per second, halved"},
        "622": {"comment":"Less the overhead of a cycle"},
        "631": {"synopsis":"Plays DE cycles with HL as the half-cycle delay\n1. The delay's two low bits pick how many of the NOPs at $028F each half cycle runs.\n2. Each half cycle waits, then flips the speaker bit and sends the border copy to port $FE.\n3. At the end the copy at $5B00 takes the final speaker bit."},
        "633": {"comment":"No cycles?"},
        "640": {"comment":"3 - the delay's two low bits"},
        "646": {"comment":"IY = the first NOP to run"},
        "655": {"synopsis":"Up to three NOPs that tune the half cycle's length; reached by JP (IY)"},
        "660": {"synopsis":"The delay loop: C counts L / 4 and B counts H"},
        "669": {"comment":"Flips the speaker bit"},
        "675": {"comment":"Speaker bit now set?"},
        "688": {"synopsis":"The first half of a cycle is over: waits for the second"},
        "692": {"synopsis":"The last cycle is over"},
        "695": {"synopsis":"Keeps the border and speaker bits of a port $FE value in the copy at $5B00\nEntry: A = the value.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "706": {"synopsis":"Gives the border and speaker bits of the port $FE copy at $5B00\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the copy's bits 0-2 and 4.\nChanges: AF."},
        "712": {"synopsis":"Ends the program: calls the handlers in the table counted at $5B0A, last first, and stops.\nNothing in this ROM adds a handler, so it just stops\nEntry: HL = the exit code (not used).","comment":"DE = the handler count; the handlers' addresses follow"},
        "717": {"comment":"No handlers?"},
        "727": {"synopsis":"Calls the next handler, going back through the table"},
        "745": {"synopsis":"Compares two blocks given on the stack, which the routine takes off: the caller pushes the\nlength, the second block's address and the first block's address, and calls\nEntry: on the stack, the first block on top, then the second, then the length.\nExit: HL = 0 when the blocks are the same, else nonzero (H = the difference of the bytes).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "753": {"synopsis":"Compares two blocks byte by byte\nEntry: DE = the first block; HL = the second; BC = the length.\nExit: HL = 0 when the blocks are the same, else nonzero (H = the difference of the bytes).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "755": {"comment":"Nothing to compare?"},
        "757": {"synopsis":"Compares the next two bytes"},
        "760": {"comment":"Bytes differ?"},
        "763": {"comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "766": {"synopsis":"The blocks are the same: HL = BC, which is 0 here"},
        "769": {"synopsis":"The blocks differ: H = the first byte - the second, nonzero"},
        "773": {"synopsis":"Copies a block\nEntry: HL = the source; DE = the destination; BC = the length.\nExit: HL = the destination; carry clear.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "775": {"comment":"Nothing to copy?"},
        "783": {"synopsis":"Nothing to copy: returns the destination"},
        "786": {"synopsis":"Fills a block with one value\nEntry: HL = the block; BC = the length; E = the value.\nExit: HL = the block.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "791": {"comment":"Nothing to fill?"},
        "797": {"comment":"Only one byte?"},
        "799": {"comment":"Each byte copies the one before it"},
        "803": {"synopsis":"Gives the length of a text ended by a zero byte\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: HL = the length, the zero byte not counted.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "814": {"synopsis":"Waits HL milliseconds: DELAY_T with 3457 T-states for each millisecond but the last, and\n3446 for the last, which also pays for this routine's own overhead\nEntry: HL = the number of milliseconds, at least 1.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "816": {"synopsis":"One millisecond"},
        "829": {"synopsis":"The last millisecond"},
        "835": {"synopsis":"Waits HL T-states, the call included, at 3.5 MHz timing\n1. 141 are taken off for the fixed part.\n2. The loop takes 23 per pass while that many remain.\n3. The branches after it make up the rest.\nEntry: HL = the T-states, at least 141.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "842": {"synopsis":"One pass of 23 T-states"},
        "856": {"synopsis":"An INC HL that only spends time, on the paths that need it"},
        "857": {"synopsis":"Spends the remainder's low three bits: a set bit 0, 1 or 2 makes its branch 1, 2 or 4\nT-states longer"},
        "858": {"comment":"Bit 0 set?"},
        "861": {"synopsis":"The remainder's bit 1"},
        "862": {"comment":"Bit 1 clear?"},
        "866": {"synopsis":"The remainder's bit 2: RET NC returns sooner when it is clear"},
        "869": {"synopsis":"Gives the cluster that follows one in the file allocation table. The table's sector is read\ninto the buffer at $5B33 unless it is the one read last (kept at $5D34)\n1. FAT32 ($5B0C nonzero): 128 entries of 4 bytes per sector; FAT16: 256 entries of 2 bytes.\n2. The sector wanted ($5D3C) is the table's start ($5B0D) plus the cluster / entries.\n3. The entry's offset within the sector goes to $5D38.\n4. A FAT32 entry's top 4 bits are dropped.\nEntry: on the stack, under the return address, the cluster as a long word (low word on top).\nExit: DEHL = the next cluster; DEHL = 0 when the sector cannot be read.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "877": {"comment":"FAT32?"},
        "901": {"comment":"The cluster / 128: seven shifts right"},
        "903": {"synopsis":"One shift right of the four bytes at $5D3C"},
        "919": {"comment":"The entry within the sector: the cluster's low 7 bits"},
        "937": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the sector is the cluster's top three bytes, the entry its low byte"},
        "971": {"synopsis":"The sector already in the buffer?"},
        "999": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector: the table's start + the sector wanted"},
        "1035": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "1045": {"synopsis":"Read: remembers the sector at $5D34"},
        "1066": {"synopsis":"Picks the entry out of the buffer"},
        "1070": {"comment":"FAT32?"},
        "1092": {"comment":"The top 4 bits dropped"},
        "1097": {"synopsis":"A FAT16 entry: 2 bytes, the high word 0"},
        "1110": {"synopsis":"Keeps the entry at $5D38-$5D3B and returns it in DEHL"},
        "1124": {"synopsis":"Returns"},
        "1127": {"synopsis":"Mounts the FAT16 or FAT32 file system on the SD card: reads its boot sector and works out\nwhere the tables, the root directory and the data are\n1. The cached table sector is forgotten; FAT16 is assumed ($5B0C = 0).\n2. Sector 0 is read. With neither file-system name in it, it is taken as a partition table:\n   the first partition's start goes to $5D40, the table's last two bytes must be $55 and $AA\n   (either order), and the partition's first sector is read.\n3. That sector must name FAT32 (then $5B0C = 1) or FAT16, end with $55 $AA, start with a\n   jump ($E9 or $EB), and have 512 bytes per sector.\n4. The geometry goes to the variables at $5B0D-$5B32 (FAT_MOUNT_GEOM, FAT_MOUNT_FAT32,\n   FAT_MOUNT_FAT16).\nEntry: none.\nExit: L = 1 when mounted, L = 0 when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "1140": {"comment":"No table sector cached yet"},
        "1149": {"comment":"FAT16 until FAT32 is found"},
        "1163": {"comment":"Sector 0 into the buffer"},
        "1168": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "1174": {"synopsis":"Sector 0 is in the buffer: the partition starts at 0 unless sector 0 is a partition table\n($5D33 = 1 until a file-system name is found)"},
        "1188": {"comment":"Is \"FAT16   \" at offset $36?"},
        "1212": {"synopsis":"Is \"FAT32   \" at offset $52?"},
        "1236": {"synopsis":"A partition table?"},
        "1252": {"comment":"The first partition's start sector, at offset $1C6"},
        "1272": {"comment":"The table's last two bytes"},
        "1280": {"comment":"$AA then $55?"},
        "1303": {"synopsis":"$55 then $AA?"},
        "1313": {"synopsis":"Not mounted"},
        "1318": {"synopsis":"Reads the partition's first sector into the buffer"},
        "1335": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "1341": {"synopsis":"Is \"FAT32   \" at offset $52?"},
        "1367": {"synopsis":"Is \"FAT16   \" at offset $36?"},
        "1391": {"synopsis":"Does the sector end with $55 $AA?"},
        "1405": {"synopsis":"No: not mounted"},
        "1410": {"synopsis":"Does the sector start with a jump?"},
        "1426": {"synopsis":"512 bytes per sector (offset $0B)?"},
        "1439": {"synopsis":"No: not mounted"},
        "1444": {"synopsis":"The geometry both file systems share\n1. $5B23 = the sectors per cluster (offset $0D); $5B27 = that - 1, a mask.\n2. $5B0D = the partition's start + the reserved sectors (offset $0E): the first table.\n3. $5B21 = the number of tables (offset $10)."},
        "1562": {"comment":"FAT32?"},
        "1569": {"synopsis":"FAT32: the root directory is a cluster chain\n1. $5B2B = the sectors per cluster * 16: the directory entries in a cluster.\n2. $5B1D = the sectors per cluster.\n3. $5B2F = the sectors per table (offset $24).\n4. $5B11 = the first table + the tables * the sectors per table: the first data sector.\n5. $5B15 = the root directory's first cluster (offset $2C), its top 4 bits dropped.\n6. $5B19 = the first data sector + (that cluster - 2) * the sectors per cluster.","comment":"\"FAT32   \" still at offset $52?"},
        "1593": {"synopsis":"Works out the FAT32 geometry"},
        "1607": {"synopsis":"One shift left of the four bytes at $5B2B"},
        "1986": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the root directory has a fixed place and size\n1. $5B2B = the root directory's entries (offset $11).\n2. $5B1D = (the entries * 32 + 511) / 512: its sectors.\n3. $5B2F = the sectors per table (offset $16).\n4. $5B19 = the first table + the tables * the sectors per table: the root directory.\n5. $5B15 = 0: no root cluster.\n6. $5B11 = the root directory + its sectors: the first data sector."},
        "2020": {"synopsis":"One shift left of the entries: 5 passes multiply by 32"},
        "2038": {"synopsis":"Adds 511 and drops the low byte; then one shift right makes it / 512"},
        "2165": {"synopsis":"Mounted"},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"Returns with L = the result"},
        "2172": {"synopsis":"Looks for a file in the root directory by its 11-character name and fills in a file record\nfor it: the sector count read so far (0), the file's size and its first cluster\n1. The directory is read a sector at a time, 16 entries of 32 bytes per sector.\n2. Unused entries (first byte 0 or $E5), volume names and directories are passed over.\n3. FAT16 looks through the fixed root directory once; FAT32 follows its cluster chain until\n   an end mark.\nEntry: on the stack, the record's address on top, the name's address under it.\nExit: L = 1 when found, L = 0 when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "2200": {"comment":"No table sector cached yet"},
        "2209": {"comment":"The directory's first cluster and first sector"},
        "2251": {"comment":"FAT32?"},
        "2269": {"synopsis":"FAT32: the entries in a cluster, the sectors per cluster * 16"},
        "2280": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the entries in the root directory, its sectors * 16"},
        "2292": {"synopsis":"One shift left of the count"},
        "2301": {"synopsis":"Keeps the count at $5D58"},
        "2311": {"synopsis":"Starts a cluster (or the FAT16 root directory): entry 0"},
        "2320": {"synopsis":"All entries looked at?"},
        "2349": {"synopsis":"The next entry: the first of a sector reads the sector"},
        "2352": {"comment":"A new sector?"},
        "2380": {"synopsis":"Reads the directory sector into the buffer; the next one goes to $5D4C"},
        "2397": {"synopsis":"The next entry in the same sector: 32 bytes on"},
        "2407": {"synopsis":"Is this the entry?"},
        "2412": {"comment":"Never used?"},
        "2416": {"comment":"Deleted?"},
        "2425": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4: a volume name or a directory?"},
        "2443": {"comment":"The name the same?"},
        "2451": {"comment":"Found: fills in the record"},
        "2485": {"comment":"The size, at offset $1C"},
        "2520": {"comment":"The first cluster's low word, at offset $1A"},
        "2531": {"comment":"FAT32?"},
        "2537": {"comment":"Its high word, at offset $14, the top 4 bits dropped"},
        "2561": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the high word is 0"},
        "2574": {"synopsis":"Stores the first cluster at the record's offset 8, and 0 at offset 0"},
        "2625": {"synopsis":"Not this entry: counts it and goes on"},
        "2647": {"synopsis":"Out of entries: the FAT16 root directory is done; FAT32 goes on to the next cluster"},
        "2661": {"comment":"The next cluster"},
        "2688": {"comment":"$0FFFFFF8 or above: the end of the chain?"},
        "2703": {"synopsis":"The cluster's first sector: the first data sector + (cluster - 2) * the sectors per cluster"},
        "2752": {"synopsis":"Not found"},
        "2754": {"synopsis":"Returns with L = the result"},
        "2759": {"synopsis":"Reads the next sector of a file found by FIND_FILE, and moves the record on\n1. The sector: the first data sector + (the cluster - 2) * the sectors per cluster + the\n   record's count masked by $5B27.\n2. The count goes up by one; when it reaches a new cluster, the record takes the next\n   cluster from the table. The end of the file is not checked.\nEntry: on the stack, the record's address on top, the buffer's address under it.\nExit: L = 1 when read, L = 0 when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "2804": {"comment":"The record's cluster, at offset 8"},
        "2870": {"comment":"The count's place within the cluster"},
        "2923": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "2928": {"synopsis":"Counts the sector"},
        "2944": {"synopsis":"Keeps the new count; is it the first sector of a cluster?"},
        "3010": {"synopsis":"Read"},
        "3012": {"synopsis":"Returns with L = the result"},
        "3017": {"synopsis":"Reports a failure and stops: a red border, the message centred on row 12, then one low beep\n(110 Hz, 125 ms) per unit of the error number, a quarter second apart\nEntry: on the stack, the message's address on top, the error number (a byte) under it.\nExit: never returns: EXIT stops the processor.\nChanges: everything."},
        "3025": {"comment":"Deselects the SD card"},
        "3029": {"comment":"Red border"},
        "3034": {"comment":"Column 16 - half the message's length, row 12"},
        "3069": {"comment":"A quarter second"},
        "3077": {"synopsis":"All the beeps given?"},
        "3104": {"synopsis":"Stops, with exit code 1"},
        "3113": {"synopsis":"The boot ROM's program: either restarts the Next with its core from flash, or loads and runs\nthe update module from TBBLUE.FW on the SD card\n1. A black screen with white text, the ULA palette, a 440 Hz beep for 300 ms.\n2. While only the M1 button is held, a countdown from 25 s (MAIN_COUNTDOWN).\n3. The text turns red; the SD card is set up and its file system mounted, three tries\n   10 ms apart (error 1).\n4. TBBLUE.FW must be on the card (error 2).\n5. Unless both the M1 and DRIVE buttons are held, the core is started from flash\n   (MAIN_BOOT_CORE).\n6. With both held, TBBLUE.TBU must be there too (error 3), and TBBLUE.FW's update module is\n   loaded and run (MAIN_READ_HDR).\nEntry: none.\nExit: never returns: the core restarts, the module runs, or an error stops it.\nChanges: everything.","comment":"Black border"},
        "3118": {"comment":"Clears the screen's pixels"},
        "3131": {"comment":"White ink on black paper"},
        "3144": {"comment":"The ULA palette"},
        "3147": {"comment":"440 Hz for 300 ms"},
        "3157": {"comment":"250 tenths of a second"},
        "3162": {"synopsis":"Counts down while only the M1 button is held: shows the seconds left at column 15, row 12,\nevery tenth of a second; letting go or pressing DRIVE as well ends it"},
        "3166": {"comment":"Time up?"},
        "3168": {"comment":"NextReg $10 (Core Boot), read through ports $243B and $253B"},
        "3178": {"comment":"Bits 1-0 = 01: M1 held, DRIVE not?"},
        "3185": {"comment":"Column 15, row 12"},
        "3193": {"comment":"The tens of seconds: the count / 100"},
        "3216": {"comment":"The seconds: (the count / 10) mod 10"},
        "3247": {"comment":"A tenth of a second"},
        "3259": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen for red text and gives the card three tries"},
        "3272": {"comment":"Red ink on black paper"},
        "3290": {"synopsis":"Sets up the card and mounts its file system"},
        "3295": {"comment":"Card set up?"},
        "3302": {"comment":"Mounted?"},
        "3304": {"synopsis":"Waits 10 ms; tries left?"},
        "3316": {"synopsis":"All three tries failed?"},
        "3322": {"comment":"Error 1: \"Error Mounting SD Card\""},
        "3335": {"synopsis":"Looks for TBBLUE.FW, its record at $5D60"},
        "3352": {"comment":"Error 2: \"TBBLUE.FW Not Found\""},
        "3365": {"synopsis":"Both the DRIVE and M1 buttons held (NextReg $10 bits 1-0 = 11)? If not, the core is started"},
        "3386": {"comment":"Looks for TBBLUE.TBU"},
        "3403": {"comment":"Error 3: \"TBBLUE.TBU Not Found\""},
        "3416": {"synopsis":"Looks for TBBLUE.FW again: its record was used for TBBLUE.TBU"},
        "3433": {"comment":"Error 2: \"TBBLUE.FW Not Found\""},
        "3446": {"synopsis":"Reads TBBLUE.FW's first sector into the buffer at $5D6C: its words at offsets 8 and 10 are\nthe sectors to pass over and the sectors of the update module"},
        "3463": {"comment":"Error 4: \"Error Reading TBBLUE.FW\""},
        "3476": {"synopsis":"$5F6D = the sectors to pass over; $5F6F = the sectors to load"},
        "3488": {"synopsis":"Reads the sectors before the module into the buffer, one by one"},
        "3502": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "3523": {"comment":"Error 4: \"Error Reading TBBLUE.FW\""},
        "3538": {"synopsis":"Loads the update module at $6000, a sector at a time"},
        "3541": {"synopsis":"Any sectors left?"},
        "3561": {"comment":"The next sector to DE"},
        "3578": {"comment":"Error 5: \"Error Loading UPDATE Module\""},
        "3592": {"synopsis":"512 bytes on"},
        "3598": {"synopsis":"Deselects the SD card and runs the module"},
        "3605": {"synopsis":"Starts the Next's core: deselects the SD card and writes $81 to NextReg $10, which sets the\nflash boot bit (7) with core number 1, so the FPGA reloads from flash. Should the program\nstill run 100 ms later, it reports error 6"},
        "3619": {"comment":"Error 6: \"Failed to Start ZX Next Core\""},
        "3633": {"synopsis":"Loads the ULA's first palette from index 0 (NextReg $43 = 0, $40 = 0): the 16 ink entries\nfrom $13E6, then the 16 paper entries from $13F6, each byte through NextReg $41\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "3643": {"synopsis":"The next ink entry; 16 done?"},
        "3662": {"synopsis":"The paper entries"},
        "3664": {"synopsis":"The next paper entry; 16 done?"},
        "3682": {"synopsis":"Sets where PRINT_CHAR prints: the column (taken mod 32) to $5F71 and the row (23 at most)\nto $5F72. The caller pushes them as one word and takes it off after\nEntry: on the stack, under the return address, a word: the column low, the row high.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "3705": {"comment":"Row past 23?"},
        "3712": {"synopsis":"Returns"},
        "3715": {"synopsis":"Prints a character at the print position from the font at $102B, and moves one column right.\nThe column does not wrap\nEntry: on the stack, under the return address, the character code (one byte), 32 to 127.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3723": {"comment":"The font"},
        "3731": {"comment":"The code - 32, times 8"},
        "3743": {"comment":"The cell at the print position"},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"Eight pixel rows, 256 bytes apart on the screen"},
        "3771": {"synopsis":"One column right"},
        "3778": {"synopsis":"Prints a text ended by a zero byte\nEntry: on the stack, under the return address, the text's address.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3792": {"synopsis":"The next character; the end?"},
        "3807": {"synopsis":"Returns"},
        "3810": {"synopsis":"Sets up the SD card in SPI mode\n1. 80 clocks with the card deselected, then the card selected, CMD12 sent and 9 bytes read.\n2. CMD0 until the card answers, at most 16 times.\n3. CMD8 with $1AA: rejected, the card is set up with CMD1; accepted, with ACMD41 asking for\n   high capacity. Either is repeated until the card is ready, at most 30720 times.\n4. CMD58 reads the card's OCR: its CCS bit says whether sectors are addressed by number\n   ($5F73 = $40) or by byte; a byte-addressed card gets CMD16, 512-byte blocks.\n5. The card is deselected.\nEntry: none.\nExit: L = 3 for a card addressed by sector, 2 for one addressed by byte, 0 for no card.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Deselects the card"},
        "3816": {"synopsis":"Ten bytes of $FF: 80 clocks"},
        "3822": {"comment":"Selects card 0"},
        "3826": {"comment":"CMD12"},
        "3833": {"synopsis":"Reads nine bytes"},
        "3839": {"synopsis":"CMD0; answered?"},
        "3861": {"synopsis":"CMD8 with $1AA; rejected?"},
        "3877": {"synopsis":"Up to 120 * 256 tries of the start-up command at HL"},
        "3880": {"synopsis":"Card ready?"},
        "3893": {"synopsis":"No card: deselects it"},
        "3900": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: CALL $0F3C runs the start-up command chosen"},
        "3901": {"synopsis":"CMD58: the OCR's first byte in B"},
        "3912": {"comment":"The CCS bit"},
        "3936": {"synopsis":"CMD16 with 512: the block length of a byte-addressed card\nEntry: none.\nExit: carry set when the card refused.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "3947": {"synopsis":"Reads one 512-byte sector with CMD17, the card left selected\n1. A byte-addressed card gets the sector number * 512.\n2. The card's data token ($FE) is waited for; the two CRC bytes after the data are dropped.\nEntry: on the stack, the sector number's low word on top, then its high word, then the\nbuffer's address.\nExit: L = 1 when read, L = 0 when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3951": {"comment":"Selects card 0"},
        "3955": {"comment":"Addressed by byte?"},
        "3962": {"comment":"CMD17"},
        "3969": {"synopsis":"Not read"},
        "3972": {"synopsis":"The data token, then 512 bytes into the buffer"},
        "3985": {"comment":"The CRC, dropped"},
        "3993": {"synopsis":"Turns a sector number into a byte address: times 512\nEntry: BC = the sector number's high word; DE = its low word.\nExit: BCDE = the byte address.\nChanges: F, BC, DE."},
        "4005": {"synopsis":"CMD1: the start-up command of a card that rejected CMD8\nEntry: none.\nExit: carry clear when the card is ready.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4007": {"synopsis":"Sends the command in A with an argument of 0\nEntry: A = the command byte.\nExit: A = the card's answer; carry set unless it is 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4012": {"synopsis":"Sends the command in A with the argument in BCDE\nEntry: A = the command byte; BCDE = the argument.\nExit: A = the card's answer; carry set unless it is 0.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "4017": {"synopsis":"Carry set: the answer was not the one wanted"},
        "4019": {"synopsis":"ACMD41 with the high-capacity bit: CMD55, then CMD41 with $40000000\nEntry: none.\nExit: carry clear when the card is ready.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4033": {"synopsis":"Sends the command in A with the argument in DE (its high word 0)\nEntry: A = the command byte; DE = the argument's low word.\nExit: A = the card's answer; carry set when it has an error bit.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4040": {"comment":"Any bit but \"idle\"?"},
        "4046": {"synopsis":"Sends the command in A with the argument in DE, then reads the four bytes that follow the\nanswer\nEntry: A = the command byte; DE = the argument's low word.\nExit: A = the card's answer; BCDE = the four bytes; carry set when it has an error bit.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4071": {"synopsis":"Sends a command: its byte, the argument high byte first, a CRC byte, then waits for the\ncard's answer. Only CMD0 and CMD8 need a correct CRC: $95 and $87; the rest get $FF\nEntry: A = the command byte; BCDE = the argument.\nExit: A = the card's answer, $FF when none came.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4091": {"comment":"CMD0?"},
        "4097": {"comment":"CMD8?"},
        "4105": {"synopsis":"Sends the CRC byte and waits for the answer"},
        "4110": {"synopsis":"Waits for the data token $FE, up to ten answers\nEntry: none.\nExit: carry clear when the token came.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "4112": {"synopsis":"The token?"},
        "4124": {"synopsis":"Reads the card until a byte other than $FF comes, at most 25600 times\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the byte, $FF when none came.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4127": {"synopsis":"Not $FF?"},
        "4138": {"synopsis":"One unused byte between the code and the font"},
        "4139": {"synopsis":"The character set: 8 bytes per character, top row first, for codes 32 to 127; code 127 is a\ncopyright sign. PRINT_CHAR finds a code's bytes at $102B + 8 * (code - 32)"},
        "4907": {"synopsis":"The texts, each ended by a zero byte: the two file-system names a boot sector is checked\nfor, the error messages, and the two file names in the 8.3 form a directory entry holds\n1. $132B \"FAT16   \" and $1334 \"FAT32   \": compared with a boot sector's file-system type\n2. $133D \"Error Mounting SD Card\": error 1\n3. $1354 \"TBBLUE  FW \" (TBBLUE.FW) and $1360 \"TBBLUE.FW Not Found\": error 2\n4. $1374 \"TBBLUE  TBU\" (TBBLUE.TBU) and $1380 \"TBBLUE.TBU Not Found\": error 3\n5. $1395 \"Error Reading TBBLUE.FW\": error 4\n6. $13AD \"Error Loading UPDATE Module\": error 5\n7. $13C9 \"Failed to Start ZX Next Core\": error 6"},
        "5094": {"synopsis":"The 32 palette bytes SET_PALETTE writes to the ULA's first palette from index 0: the eight\ncolours and then their bright forms, each as RRRGGGBB, once for the ink entries ($13E6) and\nonce again for the paper entries ($13F6)"},
        "5126": {"synopsis":"The start values of the six bytes at $5B00-$5B05, which START copies there: all $FF. $5B00\nkeeps the value last sent to port $FE"},
        "5132": {"synopsis":"Unused: $FF to the end of the 8K"}
      }
    }
  },
